
EX.NO. 11: ANALYZE AND FIX FAILING CI WORKFLOWS

AIM:
To identify, analyze, and fix errors in a failing GitHub Actions workflow and verify that the corrected workflow runs successfully.

GITHUB REPOSITORY:
https://github.com/sivapriyakumar246-cyber/GitExperiment1

STEP 1: OPEN THE REPOSITORY

Open the repository in a browser and click the Actions tab.

STEP 2: CREATE A WORKFLOW WITH AN INTENTIONAL ERROR

Open CMD and navigate to the repository:

cd "%USERPROFILE%\GitExperiment1\GitExperiment1"

Create the workflow folder if it does not exist:

mkdir .github\workflows

Open Notepad:

notepad .github\workflows\ci-fix-demo.yml

Paste this YAML into Notepad and save it:

name: CI Failure and Fix Demo

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Run test command
        run: |
          echo "Starting CI test"
          python --version
          exit 1

      - name: Finish
        run: echo "CI test completed"

STEP 3: COMMIT AND PUSH THE FAILING WORKFLOW

Run these commands separately in CMD:

git status
git add .github\workflows\ci-fix-demo.yml
git commit -m "Add CI workflow failure demonstration"
git push origin main

If Git rejects the push because GitHub has newer changes, run:

git pull --no-rebase origin main
git push origin main

STEP 4: IDENTIFY THE FAILED WORKFLOW

1. Open GitHub repository and click Actions.
2. Select CI Failure and Fix Demo.
3. Open the latest workflow run.
4. Click the failed job named test.
5. Expand the Run test command step.
6. Find the failure message.

The workflow fails because the command exit 1 returns a failure status.

Take a screenshot of the failed workflow and its log.

STEP 5: ANALYZE THE ERROR

The failing command is:

exit 1

Exit status 1 indicates that the command failed. GitHub Actions marks the job as failed when a step returns a non-zero exit code.

STEP 6: FIX THE WORKFLOW

Open the workflow file:

notepad .github\workflows\ci-fix-demo.yml

Replace the failing command:

exit 1

with:

echo "Test passed"

The corrected Run test command step should be:

      - name: Run test command
        run: |
          echo "Starting CI test"
          python --version
          echo "Test passed"

Save and close Notepad.

STEP 7: COMMIT AND PUSH THE FIX

Run these commands in CMD:

git add .github\workflows\ci-fix-demo.yml
git commit -m "Fix failing CI workflow"
git push origin main

If Git rejects the push because GitHub has newer changes, run:

git pull --no-rebase origin main
git push origin main

STEP 8: VERIFY THE CORRECTED WORKFLOW

1. Open GitHub repository and click Actions.
2. Open CI Failure and Fix Demo.
3. Select the latest run created by the fix commit.
4. Check that the job finishes with a green Success status.
5. Open the job logs and confirm the test step completed.

Take a screenshot of the successful workflow run.

STEP 9: RESULT

The CI workflow failure was analyzed by examining its logs. The incorrect failing command was identified and corrected. After committing and pushing the fix, the GitHub Actions workflow completed successfully.
